From 83992fe62ac26252622ca888421602abafe20b44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:45:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] dadao: remove additional pre-existing K3 O0
 bool-carrier workarounds (KL-153a)

KL-153a's task scope enumerated 10 Linux-side bool-widening commits
(bd10b11e2..3e83c7744) as the complete set needing removal after the
LLVM DADAO -O0 i1 stack-slot root cause was fixed. A tree-wide grep for
CONFIG_DADAO_K3_O0_LINK_COMPAT and the "_result_t"/"_match_t" carrier
typedef convention found 8 more instances predating that list, from
even earlier K3 bring-up work (06c3d571a "harden K3 O0 early boot
progress", 537c61bae "complete K3 mem_init progress", 4f32b2dd2
"complete K3 mm_init progress" -- each of those commits mixes a
legitimate, unrelated change with a bool-carrier workaround, so they
are hand-edited here rather than reverted wholesale):

- include/linux/mm.h: want_init_on_alloc/want_init_on_free
  (page_init_result_t, from 06c3d571a)
- include/linux/moduleparam.h + kernel/params.c: parameq/parameqn/
  param_check_unsafe (kernel_param_match_t, from 06c3d571a)
- init/main.c: obsolete_checksetup (obsolete_setup_result_t, from
  06c3d571a)
- kernel/locking/mutex.c: __mutex_trylock/__mutex_trylock_fast/
  __mutex_unlock_fast (mutex_fast_result_t, from 06c3d571a)
- kernel/printk/printk.c: cont_add (printk_cont_result_t, from
  06c3d571a)
- mm/memblock.c: should_skip_region (memblock_skip_region_t, from
  06c3d571a)
- mm/page_alloc.c: free_pages_prepare/free_pcp_prepare/
  free_unref_page_prepare (free_pages_result_t, from 537c61bae)
- mm/page_alloc.c: prepare_alloc_pages (prepare_alloc_pages_result_t,
  from 4f32b2dd2)

Each site is restored to a plain `bool` return type with the carrier
typedef and its guarding #ifdef CONFIG_DADAO_K3_O0_LINK_COMPAT deleted.
CONFIG_DADAO_K3_O0_LINK_COMPAT itself, arch/dadao/mm/o0-link-compat.c,
and the one legitimate non-carrier use of the config
(include/linux/huge_mm.h's disabled-feature HPAGE_PMD_* macro
fallback) are untouched -- confirmed by grep, only that single
CONFIG_DADAO_K3_O0_LINK_COMPAT reference remains tree-wide outside
o0-link-compat.c itself.

A fresh KCFLAGS=-O0 Image build after this commit plus the preceding
10 reverts succeeds cleanly (no new errors, no "shift count is
negative" / ELF_CLASS diagnostics), and llvm-objdump on the resulting
vmlinux confirms node_tag_get itself (the KL-153a anchor site) now
emits `stb`/`ldbu` at rb1+31, not `stb`/`ldo`.
